WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.270
CONFESSION

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.430
CONFESSION

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:05.730
<i>You fall in love with someone...</i>

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.020
P-Please be my girlfriend!

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.480
<i>confess that love...</i>

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.110
<i>and become a couple.</i>

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.120
<i>Everyone would say that's a wonderful thing.</i>

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.040
<i>But they're wrong!</i>

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.960
<i>Even among sweethearts,
there exists a distinct power relationship!</i>

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.420
<i>A side that exploits
and a side that's exploited,</i>

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.590
<i>a side that's devoted,
a side receiving devotion,</i>

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.510
<i>a winner and a loser!</i>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.020
<i>If you're trying to live a noble life,
then you mustn't become a loser!</i>

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.640
<i>Love is war!</i>

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:46.270
CONFESSION

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.520
CONFESSION

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.820
<i>The person who falls in love loses!</i>

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.030
KAGUYA-SAMA: LOVE IS WAR

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.620
<i>Shuchiin Academy!</i>

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:33.380
<i>It's a prestigious school
with an ancient and honorable origin,</i>

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.630
<i>founded as a facility
to educate upper-crust children.</i>

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.550
<i>The focus on the nobility is gone,</i>

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.930
<i>but many talented students
born into wealthy, distinguished families,</i>

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.010
<i>and shouldering the future
attend the school.</i>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.350
And now a message
from the student council.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.020
The student council members.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.730
<i>Naturally ordinary people wouldn't be permitted
to lead and bring these students together!</i>

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.490
<i>Kaguya Shinomiya, the vice-president
of the student council at Shuchiin Academy.</i>

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.160
<i>Total assets: 200 trillion yen.</i>

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.700
<i>Her family owns the Shinomiya Group,</i>

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:09.580
<i>one of the top four financial conglomerates
in Japan, with over 1,000 subsidiaries.</i>

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.870
SHINOMIYA BANK

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.540
<i>Befitting her superior lineage,
she's a talented young woman</i>

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.000
<i>who has attained
splendid achievements in various fields,</i>

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.710
<i>such as traditional performing arts,
music and martial arts.</i>

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.510
<i>That is Kaguya Shinomiya.</i>

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.470
<i>And the young man Shinomiya supports is...</i>

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.600
<i>Miyuki Shirogane, the president
of the student council at Shuchiin Academy.</i>

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.020
<i>He's wise and intelligent,
strong and silent.</i>

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.730
<i>He scores first place
in the practice exams!</i>

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.110
<i>In contrast to talented Kaguya,</i>

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.610
<i>his devotion to studying
commands awe and fear,</i>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.940
<i>and because of that exemplary behavior,</i>

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:44.370
PRESIDENT OF STUDENT COUNCIL

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.110
<i>he was selected to be
the student council president,</i>

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:43.740
<i>despite being relatively new to the school.</i>

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.700
<i>The weight of a solid gold braided cord
has been passed down</i>

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.580
<i>from president to president
at Shuchiin Academy for 200 years!</i>

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.370
That's all!

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.300
They always look so cool!

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:05.640
Yes, when they're together,
they seem even more noble and elegant!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.970
I still wonder if they're dating.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:11.640
What? I'd be shocked if they were!

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:16.110
I always wonder what they talk about
in the student council room.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:19.780
STUDENT COUNCIL ROOM

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.530
P-President!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.360
WHAT WOULD YOU DO?

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.240
You finally bought a smartphone?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:29.030
KAGUYA WANTS TO TRADE

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:31.790
GLITTER

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.370
It's got Line, too.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.990
Then let's exchange ID's!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.790
<i>It's the age of I.T.!</i>

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.790
Cheap cell phone! It's got a cheap SIM card!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.120
<i>Even Shirogane, a stubborn cheapskate</i>

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.040
<i>who's long insisted
that smartphones are unnecessary,</i>

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.540
- Trendy! Trendy!
- I'll send it over to you by Line.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.170
<i>has finally given in and gotten one.</i>

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.170
GLITTER

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:43.130
<i>It doesn't even need to be said how important
smartphones are for high school life.</i>

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:40.920
Very nice.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.550
I love how you can do so many things with it.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:46.390
<i>You can use them for social plans
or just idly chatting,</i>

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:49.220
<i>but sometimes you may not get a reply,
so joy can swing to sorrow.</i>

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.060
<i>It's possible to confess love to someone
using the Line social app.</i>

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.560
<i>Yes! This past half-year was wasted,
because he wasn't using Line!</i>

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.320
<i>All right, ask me for my ID
anytime, Shinomiya!</i>

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.200
Yay! I got your ID!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.820
<i>Why hasn't she asked me?
It's my personal information!</i>

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.080
<i>Never mind. Should I just ask her?</i>

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.500
<i>But...</i>

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.120
<i>Asking for contact information,
between the lines,</i>

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.710
<i>that indicates a degree of desperation
and ulterior motive,</i>

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.590
<i>which then beget a special meaning...</i>

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:24.090
<i>That meaning is, in fact, love!</i>

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.760
<i>In a romantic relationship, "the person
who falls in love loses" is an absolute rule!</i>

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.350
<i>Confirming your love for someone
equals defeat!</i>

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:35.350
<i>Asking the opposite sex for their contact
information is as good as a confession of love!</i>

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.400
<i>Apparently, the president
is in love with the vice-president!</i>

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.610
<i>Seriously? I have to share that!</i>

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.490
<i>For a boy going through puberty,
that means death!</i>

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.450
<i>Forget it!</i>

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.240
<i>There's no way I can ask her!</i>

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.620
<i>Shinomiya, you ask me!</i>

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:56.290
<i>I'm sure the president is waiting for me
to ask him, but he'd better not hold his breath.</i>

00:05:56.290 --> 00:06:02.420
<i>It would mean something if he came to me
and asked, even though he was embarrassed.</i>

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.760
<i>Conflict! It's an inevitability in this world.</i>

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.300
<i>Kill or be killed!</i>

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.300
<i>Your contact info...</i>

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.050
<i>Ask for it or be asked for it?</i>

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.930
<i>It would be no overstatement to say therein
lies the person's superiority or inferiority!</i>

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:20.860
<i>Good grief. How much trouble does he think
I went to just to make sure he got a phone?</i>

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.020
Cheap cell phone!
It's got a cheap SIM card!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:21.270
SHINOMIYA
HOUSE COOK

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:21.270
KAGUYA'S ATTENDANT

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.600
- Trendy! Trendy!
- I'll send it over to you by Line.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.270
SHINOMIYA HOUSE GARDENER

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.610
<i>I can finally contact the president
outside of school.</i>

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.110
<i>I can say that my plan was a success,
by and large.</i>

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.120
<i>I see. She wants to make me,
the man, ask her!</i>

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:36.160
<i>If that's how she wants to play it...</i>

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.630
President, this profile photo...

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.670
Yeah, it's a photo of me
from when I was a kid.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.670
It's cute! You even scowled as a kid!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.760
<i>A photo of the president
from his childhood?</i>

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:51.760
You know how to hurt a guy.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.890
But that photo is a little embarrassing.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.100
<i>I-I'm not especially interested.</i>

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.020
I think I'll change it to a different one.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.430
I'll change it in three minutes.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:06:59.980
<i>What?</i>

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:05.190
<i>If the president changes his profile picture,
I'll never be able to see that photo!</i>

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:07.490
<i>But asking him for his contact info</i>

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:11.530
<i>expresses nothing other than
"I want to talk to you anytime"!</i>

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:16.160
<i>It means "I want to send
casual messages before bedtime"...</i>

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.540
<i>or "I want to talk to you on the phone...</i>

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.710
<i>in the wee hours
the night before a test and chat"!</i>

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.710
<i>It'd be like that's what I was thinking!</i>

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:30.470
<i>A lady must not do anything as improper
as asking a male for his contact information!</i>

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:33.090
<i>Since it's come to this,
I'll have to use my last resort!</i>

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.020
Kaguya?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.820
The president is so cruel.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:46.690
DRIP

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:51.780
H-How could you be so mean?

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.120
<i>Her skill of deception has been activated!</i>

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.160
A MAIDEN’S TEARS

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.490
ACTIVATED

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.490
You're terrible, President!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.540
You're terrible!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.830
<i>Her words don't especially mean anything.</i>

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.960
<i>But being told he's mean makes him
feel like he's done something mean.</i>

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.500
BARNUM EFFECT

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.500
<i>In psychology,
it's called the "Barnum Effect."</i>

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.510
I'm sorry! I didn't mean to leave you out!

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.840
Here, I'll show you too, Shinomiya!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.300
- Wait. You...
- Too late!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.010
<i>She memorized it!</i>

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.600
<i>Though it was a fleeting glimpse,
Shirogane's profile photo</i>

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.520
<i>has been preserved
in Kaguya's hippocampus!</i>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.520
<i>Shirogane lost the sole ace up his sleeve!</i>

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.900
<i>Kaguya made a comeback
to win overwhelmingly!</i>

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:36.320
<i>Now, I have no reason
to ask the president for his ID.</i>

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.200
<i>Go ahead. Ask me for mine.</i>

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.910
<i>Can I... Can I come up with anything else?</i>

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.630
<i>Shirogane racked his brain
to come from behind!</i>

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.380
<i>I guess I'll have to use that!</i>

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.460
<i>Kaguya realized that she needed
to block that line of thinking!</i>

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:52.340
<i>He's dead.</i>

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:53.590
<i>The conclusion is at hand!</i>

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.180
That's right!

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:02.060
It's cruel to talk about using Line when
Kaguya's old phone doesn't support that app!

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.190
I'm sorry!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.940
- It can't use it?
- It can't use it?

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.020
You're rich! Buy a different phone!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.980
I've used this phone ever since kindergarten,
so I'm attached to it!

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.320
I can't switch it now!

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:17.950
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.900
Get rid of your weird hang-up!

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:17.950
<i>This is a story of love and intellect
going around in circles.</i>

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:15.530
How is it weird?

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.950
BOTH LOSE

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.950
- I don't know if it's weird.
- You're weird, President!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:21.950
THEY HAVE EXCHANGED ADDRESSES.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.460
It's cold today.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.880
I wish summer would get here soon.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:30.790
CHIKA WANTS
TO GO SOMEWHERE

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.210
Talk about impatient.
It'll be spring for a long time yet.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:34.220
Oh no! Time flies by way too fast!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.140
If you're careless, you'll graduate
with nothing happening at all!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.470
80 DAMAGE TO THE HEARTS
OF SHINOMIYA AND SHIROGANE

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.100
Over the summer,
let's go on a student council trip!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.310
That's a good idea.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.810
Let's go somewhere
like an informal social gathering.

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.060
Yay!

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.400
<i>A trip, huh?</i>

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.480
<i>Then the mountains would be good.</i>

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.650
<i>Fresh air.</i>

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.820
<i>Reverberating echoes.</i>

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.370
SUMMIT

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.120
<i>We'll rent a cottage and have a barbecue.</i>

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.630
<i>At night, the starry sky will put a spell on us.</i>

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:18.130
<i>Look. There's Deneb, Altair and Vega,
the Summer Triangle.</i>

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.140
<i>Altair and Vega represent
the story of Hikoboshi and Orihime.</i>

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.430
<i>They're just like us.</i>

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.140
<i>Close together...</i>

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.650
<i>but so far apart.</i>

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:40.700
VEGA

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.370
DENEB

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.370
ALTAIR

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:44.160
<i>No! President, I want to be Bb
to your Alpha Centauri B!</i>

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.200
<i>Please let me revolve
around you, President!</i>

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.750
<i>Oh, boy.</i>

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.250
<i>You're a pampered first-magnitude star.</i>

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.000
BOOM

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.000
<i>That's it!</i>

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:57.010
<i>It has to be the mountains!</i>

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.800
Yes. If we're going, then—

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.340
It has to be the sea.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.390
Wha—

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:04.970
<i>The sea versus the mountains!</i>

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:08.270
<i>The polar opposites that people
have been fighting over since ancient times.</i>

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:11.400
<i>The curtain rises
on human nature's battle of thoughts.</i>

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.610
<i>The sea. The sea is the origin of life.</i>

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:19.610
<i>As the sun sets there, I'm sure humans
return to being creatures of instinct.</i>

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.160
<i>My swimsuit will bewitch the president
the second he sees it!</i>

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.250
<i>The sea will cast its spell
on the president,</i>

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:34.920
<i>and he'll confess his love to me
while the sun sets.</i>

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:38.260
<i>Perfect.</i>

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.430
The roar of the sea
is the best lullaby in the world.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.140
And the salty sea breeze
will blow away the summer heat.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:45.930
<i>The sea?</i>

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.890
<i>The sea is the last place I'll go!</i>

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.100
<i>I can't swim!</i>

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.140
NOTE: SINKS LIKE A HAMMER

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.270
<i>If I went into the water
with a swimming ring...</i>

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.730
<i>I didn't know you were
a hopeless swimmer, President.</i>

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:01.320
<i>How cute.</i>

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.450
<i>No way! It has to be the mountains!</i>

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.780
<i>I refuse to go to the sea!</i>

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.200
The beach would be too crowded.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.790
I hate bumping elbows with strangers.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:12.500
Let's use a private beach
owned by my family.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:15.040
It has warm showers, too.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.130
Sunburn is a young lady's archenemy!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.840
I'll bring along the highest grade sunscreen.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.880
And to seal the deal, I'll hire
a first-class aesthetician for skin aftercare.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:28.220
- There might be sharks.
- I'll hire a first-class hunter from Florida.

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:29.810
Then we can have shark fin soup.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:29.810
COMFY

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.980
<i>Damn you, rich girl!</i>

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.560
<i>Weak sauce, President.</i>

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:42.570
THINGS THE PRESIDENT IS LIKELY TO SAY,
VOL. 42, TRIP EDITION

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:40.190
<i>I've already turned out a series of manuals
to prepare for when you oppose me.</i>

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:42.570
<i>However you attack me,
I can render it harmless.</i>

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.820
We can only go to the sea
in the summer, right?

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.030
With mountains,
you can't depend on weather.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.370
It rains a lot.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.950
Besides, it's got a lot of bugs.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:53.540
<i>Bugs!</i>

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:59.420
Moths, mosquitoes, horseflies, centipedes,
ladybugs, earthworms, drone beetles...

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.170
<i>Bugs are the only thing.</i>

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.880
<i>Bugs are the only thing I can't stand!</i>

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.800
NOTE: HATES BUGS

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.550
<i>What should I do?
If I go to the sea, I can't swim.</i>

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.430
<i>If I go to the mountains,
there are insects!</i>

00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:14.560
Guess I'll buy a swimsuit.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.730
<i>I won!</i>

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.190
That's right.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.270
My swimsuit from last year
doesn't fit me now.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.690
I have to buy a new one.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.620
FLAT

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.120
<i>Normally, Shinomiya
has confidence in her body line.</i>

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:40.960
<i>But take that away,
and her offensive ability becomes fragile...</i>

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.460
<i>Pop.</i>

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.090
<i>on the level of a peashooter.</i>

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:47.300
<i>On the other hand, Chika Fujiwara's
offensive ability is tank-class.</i>

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.300
<i>The difference
in military strength is hopeless.</i>

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.760
<i>This is bad!
Never mind about enchanting him!</i>

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.600
<i>What is that?</i>

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:59.270
<i>Compared to that, Shinomiya is...
How can I put it?</i>

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:02.270
<i>She has a cute chest?</i>

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:05.280
<i>Cute?</i>

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.030
Let's go to the mountains.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.030
The beach is too crowded,
and there are sharks.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:13.290
- Let's go to the mountains.
- You didn't say that before!

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.540
No, the sea!

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.460
It rains in the mountains, and there are
lots of bugs! Let's go to the sea!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:18.290
You, too?

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.830
- The mountains.
- The sea.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.670
- Mountains.
- Sea.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:21.590
- Mountains.
- Sea.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:22.420
- Mountains.
- Sea.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.210
Since it's come to this,
have Chika Fujiwara decide!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.550
Me?

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:27.760
Yes, let's do it that way.

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.300
<i>The sea. Got it?</i>

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:33.930
<i>The mountains!
You wouldn't betray me, would you?</i>

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.430
U-Um...

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.730
If I have to choose one...

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.020
The mountains?

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:42.020
Yes!

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.730
But I specifically want to go...

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.200
to Mount Osore!

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.320
Mount Osore?

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.450
Children's Limbo and Blood Pond.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.960
There are pinwheels
symbolizing death and rebirth.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:02.460
And as long as we're there,
let's have a medium channel a spirit.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.210
Who would be good?

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.170
Christ? Buddha?

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:08.260
Well, I guess we can think about it
when summer comes.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:08.260
Prince Shotoku could be good, too.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:14.140
Aristotle, Shakespeare, Cleopatra,
Einstein, Hideyoshi Toyotomi, Gandhi,

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:10.470
I agree.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:12.970
<i>Today's match...</i>

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.390
<i>Ruined.</i>

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:18.980
Sen no Rikyu, Caesar, Marie Antoinette,
Oscar Francois de Jarjayes!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.980
BECAUSE CHIKA FUJIWARA
IS A LITTLE SCARY

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:22.940
CHIKA FUJIWARA

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.440
Romantic advice?

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.400
Yes! Where romance is concerned,

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.820
I thought a veteran like you...

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:33.070
could give me advice, President!

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:35.030
MIYUKI WANTS TO HIDE
HIS IGNORANCE

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:38.200
I see.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.290
I'll help you somehow.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.250
President!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:45.290
<i>A romantic veteran?</i>

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:47.880
<i>How did people get that image of me?</i>

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.130
<i>Miyuki Shirogane, 17 years old.
Dating experience...</i>

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:52.590
<i>None.</i>

00:15:51.930 --> 00:16:03.480
NOTE: VIRGIN

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.890
<i>What? If this advice exposes me...</i>

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.930
<i>The president is a virgin.</i>

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:00.390
<i>A virgin?</i>

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.350
<i>I'm so disillusioned!</i>

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:05.480
Sh-Shinomiya!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.820
How cute.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.570
<i>No! I have to get through this!</i>

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.860
If it's about love, leave it to me!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.530
I've never been rejected before!

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.080
That's why you're the president.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.700
<i>He's never confessed his love,
so that's not actually a lie.</i>

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:23.460
<i>The president is giving advice about love?</i>

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:26.790
<i>This could be my chance
to hear his views on love!</i>

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.170
So, what's the problem?

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:36.510
KASHIWAGI

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:33.550
I have a classmate, Kashiwagi.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.510
I want to confess my love to her!

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:38.430
<i>Oh!</i>

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:41.180
But when I imagine her rejecting me,

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:44.810
I think maybe I should
become friends with her first.

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.400
Incidentally,
have you talked to her before?

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:51.280
She gave me chocolate
on Valentine's Day!

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.110
What kind of chocolate?

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:55.660
Choco Balls. Three pieces.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.030
Is that obligatory gift chocolate?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.040
<i>Obligatory gift chocolate at best!</i>

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:05.000
Yeah, I would say...

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.920
she's definitely in love with you!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:08.670
<i>Why?</i>

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.300
<i>He got Choco Balls!</i>

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.510
Listen!

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:14.050
Women are creatures
who aren't upfront about their feelings!

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:16.930
Think of it as behaving
the exact opposite of how they feel!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.180
The Choco Balls seem
like a throwaway, but...

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.180
GASP

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.060
It means she likes me?

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.180
<i>What about opposites?</i>

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.640
<i>All right! That sounded
like half-decent advice!</i>

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:28.400
But I don't think
she does feel that way about me.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.270
Just the other day...

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.780
<i>Hey, do you have a girlfriend?</i>

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.620
<i>No, but...</i>

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.530
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.330
<i>He said he doesn't have a girlfriend!</i>

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:45.410
BOOM

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.620
<i>He doesn't look like he has one!</i>

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:44.660
<i>That's hilarious!</i>

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:52.380
So, I think she was just making fun of me.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.170
<i>It's unfortunate,
but she was making fun of him.</i>

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:58.590
<i>The issue is whether she even sees him
as a member of the opposite sex.</i>

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.930
You're in your popular phase right now.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.730
Why are you so suspicious of women?

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:09.400
Woman are humans, just like you!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.940
<i>That's not what you were saying before!</i>

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:11.690
I'll make that situation
easier to understand!

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.070
<i>Hey, do you have a girlfriend?</i>

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.320
If you don't, I wanna go out with you.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:21.410
<i>No, but...</i>

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:22.620
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.370
<i>You and I are connected
by the string of fate!</i>

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.830
<i>He said he doesn't have a girlfriend!</i>

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:30.500
BOOM

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.120
<i>He doesn't look like he has one!</i>

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.500
THUMP-THUMP

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.000
<i>After all, he's too high-class!</i>

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:34.000
BOOM

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.460
<i>That's hilarious!</i>

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.000
THUMP-THUMP

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:34.210
<i>I'm thrilled that he's available!</i>

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.220
BOOM

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.220
THUMP-THUMP

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.220
<i>I'm the one who's most worthy of him.</i>

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:39.470
<i>Isn't that thinking too positively?</i>

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.930
It can't be!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.390
<i>Exactly!</i>

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:47.810
I have to choose only one of them?

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.850
<i>You're an idiot, too?</i>

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:54.070
Won't that cause a rift
in their friendship with each other?

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:57.280
Worst case, it could lead to bullying.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.200
That's what female friendship is like.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.070
<i>What is this arrogant conversation?</i>

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.830
But it'll be okay.
Because she'll have you.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.250
All you have to do is protect her.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:12.330
I can... protect her?

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.550
- President!
- Yes.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:15.590
<i>What is this?</i>

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.340
This'll be my first time
confessing my love to someone.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.130
How should I go about it?

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.970
I have a good idea.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.850
- Imagine the girl in question is right here.
- Okay.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:28.850
You do...

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.020
this!

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.230
Go out with me.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:42.740
When you suddenly corner a girl
against the wall like that, she'll be nervous,

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:44.870
but the moment
you whisper of love in her ear,

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:48.120
anxiety will turn into a throbbing heart.
Your chance of success will go up!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.580
<i>He startled me!</i>

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:54.750
I call this technique "wall-down."

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.880
I came up with it myself.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.130
<i>It's "wall-slamming”!
It's been around for years!</i>

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:01.510
SHIVER SHIVER

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.050
Genius.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.510
<i>You're that stupid?</i>

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.260
Thank you!
You've given me courage, President!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.520
I knew the person who conquered
Shinomiya could help me!

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:13.650
No, Shinomiya and I aren't dating.

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:16.770
<i>Th-That's right!
No one's ever conquered me!</i>

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:18.280
Really?

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:21.030
It seems like you two are a couple.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.660
No, just the opposite.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:26.530
Recently, I wonder if she hates me.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.160
I don't even think she's interested in me.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.500
<i>I don't especially hate you.</i>

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.290
<i>Did I do something to give you that idea?</i>

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:35.540
<i>She has no self-awareness.</i>

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:39.760
President!
What's important is how you feel!

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.140
How do I feel about Shinomiya?

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.850
Well, to be honest, her wealth
and natural talents annoy me.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:58.690
She's ditsier than you'd think,
scary in private, and her chest...

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.280
But maybe those are all good points!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:05.030
She's actually cute! A beauty!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:09.950
Refined, elegant and clever, too!
Really, she's too perfect!

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:14.120
Yeah, Shinomiya is the ideal woman!

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:20.000
<i>That was close! She's right there!</i>

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.210
<i>Thank God I noticed!</i>

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:25.340
Anyway, nothing will happen
unless you tell her how you feel!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:28.850
And nothing good can come
of carrying out some weird scheme!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:32.680
<i>Huh? Why do these words resonate with me?</i>

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:36.190
I-I'll do my best!

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.980
Thank you so much!

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.160
Kaguya.

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:51.120
Has something good happened?

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:53.580
No, nothing.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:55.920
<i>Afterwards...</i>

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:01.710
<i>he confessed his feelings to Kashiwagi,</i>

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:04.170
<i>and somehow
they're apparently a couple now.</i>

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:11.390
President, I poured you some tea.

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:14.180
Oh, thanks.

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.480
<i>Thankfully, she seems to be
in a good mood.</i>

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:20.190
<i>Today's match...</i>

00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:20.770
Is that your one smile
of the day?

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.440
<i>Kaguya wasn't particularly at fault...</i>

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:23.360
No, I'm like this
all the time.

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:24.320
<i>when Shirogane put her in a foul mood,
then a good mood,</i>

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:24.320
Oh.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:27.950
<i>but he largely wasted his efforts,
resulting in a loss for himself.</i>

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:29.950
THE NEXT PERSON SEEKING ADVICE

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:29.950
Shock!
